# Renders in GitHub's "Cite this repository" sidebar widget.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Luxas: an autonomous research agent for end-to-end literature survey, experiment design, and LaTeX report generation"
message: "If you use Luxas to produce reports for publication or as a subject of study about agentic research systems, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mu
    family-names: Qiao
    email: mu.q.phys@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Université Paris-Saclay"
    alias: Muuuun
repository-code: "https://github.com/Muuuun/luxas"
url: "https://luxas.im"
abstract: >-
  Luxas is an open-source multi-agent system for autonomous scientific research.
  Given a one-line research topic, it crawls the literature (OpenAlex, arXiv,
  CrossRef, paywalled venues via an anti-detect browser), designs and runs
  experiments under a blind impl/test split, generates publication-grade
  figures, writes a LaTeX report, submits it to adversarial content + figure +
  layout review, and produces a compiled PDF with real citations. Built on
  pi-mono primitives, the harness is file-backed and crash-recoverable, runs
  for multiple hours unattended, and supports family-wide redirect across
  Claude (Anthropic), DeepSeek-v4, Kimi (Moonshot), and OpenAI o3 via a
  single environment variable.
keywords:
  - autonomous-agent
  - multi-agent-system
  - research-agent
  - agentic-ai
  - large-language-models
  - claude
  - deepseek
  - latex
  - automated-scientific-research
  - literature-survey
